---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { api } from '../lib/api';
import { usd } from '../lib/format';

const [meta, network, policyDoc] = await Promise.all([api.meta(), api.network(), api.policy()]);
const p = policyDoc?.policy;

const promises = [
  {
    title: 'You can always take your money back',
    body: 'There is no lock-up, no notice period and no queue. We keep a slice of every balance free at all times, so a withdrawal is not waiting on anyone — including us.',
  },
  {
    title: 'We cannot move your money anywhere else',
    body: 'Your savings sit in an account that belongs to you. We can suggest a move; the account only accepts the ones that fit the rules below. There is no button, ours or anyone else\'s, that pays money out to a third party.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Only places that pass the checklist',
    body: 'We watch every place that pays for dollars. Before any money goes in, it has to be big enough for you to leave quickly, audited, and paying something we can explain. Right now most of the list does not pass, and we say so on the page instead of quietly ranking it.',
  },
  {
    title: 'If a place starts looking bad, new money stops going there',
    body: 'A problem is caught before it becomes a headline: that place stops receiving money immediately, your existing money can still be taken out, and the page tells you it happened.',
  },
  {
    title: 'Nothing moves without a reason you can read',
    body: 'Every move we make, and every move we decided not to make, is written down with the rate it was based on and the reason in plain words. You do not have to trust our judgement; you can read it.',
  },
];

const rules = [
  ['Any single place', p ? `${(p.max_venue_bps / 100).toFixed(0)}% of a balance at most` : 'a minority of a balance'],
  ['Always free to withdraw', p ? `at least ${(p.min_idle_bps / 100).toFixed(0)}%` : 'a slice kept free'],
  ['One move at a time', p ? `${(p.max_move_bps / 100).toFixed(0)}% of a balance at most` : 'a fraction of a balance'],
  ['How much better the new place must pay', p ? `at least ${(p.min_improvement_bps / 100).toFixed(2)}% more` : 'a clear improvement'],
  ['Wait between moves', p ? `${p.cooldown_secs / 86400} days` : 'a few days'],
  ['A move may never make you worse off', 'if it would, it is cancelled'],
  ['Smallest position worth opening', p ? usd(p.min_capacity_usd) : '—'],
];

const honest = [
  'Rates move. The number you see today is the rate being paid now, not a rate you are promised.',
  'A lending market can be exploited, paused, or stop paying. We size positions so that a single failure costs you a slice, never everything.',
  'A dollar coin can, in the worst case, lose its peg or be frozen by its issuer. That risk is real and it is on the page, not in a footnote.',
  'We do not take currency risk on your behalf. If you want the higher rates other countries pay, the next section is the honest version of that trade.',
];
---
<Base
  title="Why your money is safe with us"
  subtitle="Not because we say so — because of what we are structurally unable to do, and what you can check."
  network={network}
  meta={meta}
>
  <div class="grid g2 stack">
    <div class="card">
      <h2>Five promises</h2>
      <ul class="promises">
        {promises.map((x) => (
          <li>
            <span class="tick">✓</span>
            <div>
              <strong>{x.title}</strong>
              <p class="small muted">{x.body}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="card" id="rules">
      <h2>The rules we keep</h2>
      <p class="small muted">
        These are the house rules, and they are applied automatically to every move. They exist so that being
        automatic never means being careless.
      </p>
      <div class="kv small">
        {rules.map(([k, v]) => (
          <div><span>{k}</span><span class="num">{v}</span></div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="small muted mt">
        The two-day wait and the small improvement threshold are not caution for its own sake: we measured how long
        one place tends to stay ahead of another, and moving faster than that earned less than the moves cost.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="card stack callout">
    <h2>What we will not pretend</h2>
    <ul class="no">
      {honest.map((h) => <li>{h}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="small muted">
      Keelson is not a bank account and is not insured like one. Nothing here is investment or legal advice.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card stack">
    <h2>If you want the higher rates other countries pay</h2>
    <div class="grid g2">
      <div>
        <p class="small">
          Some countries pay far more than yours. We think you deserve to see those numbers — and to see the whole
          trade, not just the flattering half of it. So we publish what a dollar actually earned there over the last
          twelve months, after the currency moved.
        </p>
        <p class="small muted">
          What we will not do is pretend you can already take your money there through us. Getting a deposit into
          another country means a local bank or a licensed product, capital controls the high-rate countries impose
          when it suits them, and tax where you live. That is the next thing to solve, and until it is solved this
          page will not claim it.
        </p>
        <a class="link small" href="../borders/">The honest comparison →</a>
      </div>
      <div class="quote">
        <p>
          “A headline rate is not a return. The second number — what the currency did — is the one nobody puts in the
          advert.”
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  .stack { margin-top: 14px; }
  .promises { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; font-size: 13.5px; }
  .promises li { display: flex; gap: 10px; padding: 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px dashed #F3EBDB; }
  .promises li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .promises strong { font-size: 14px; }
  .promises p { margin: 3px 0 0; }
  .tick { color: var(--brand); font-weight: 700; flex: none; }
  .kv { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .kv div { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 14px; border-bottom: 1px dashed #F3EBDB; padding: 7px 0; }
  .kv span:first-child { color: var(--muted); }
  .kv div:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .mt { margin-top: 12px; }
  .callout { background: #FFFCF6; border-color: #E8DCC6; }
  .no { margin: 0 0 10px 18px; padding: 0; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.75; color: #4A3D2C; }
  .quote { background: var(--brand-soft); border-radius: 14px; padding: 18px; display: grid; place-items: center; }
  .quote p { margin: 0; font-family: "Iowan Old Style", Palatino, Georgia, serif; font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.45; color: var(--brand-ink); }
</style>
